pkix-path/src/lib.rs:658–660

    /// OID for the anyPolicy wildcard (2.5.29.32.0 — a child of id-ce-certificatePolicies).
    #[allow(dead_code)] // used by the policy state machine in a future child issue
    const OID_ANY_POLICY: der::asn1::ObjectIdentifier = ...;

The comment says 'used by the policy state machine in a future child issue', but OID_ANY_POLICY is already referenced at 15 locations in the same file (lines 732, 734, 1598, 1642, 1789, 1790, 1823, 1842, 2062, 2070, 2094, 2118, 2131, 2136, 2154).  The allow(dead_code) attribute is now stale — the constant is clearly in use and the compiler would not warn about it.

Remove the allow(dead_code) and update the comment to remove the 'future child issue' note.
